    {
      "id": 1,
      "title": "Lane Definitions Reference",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 5
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Lane 1 \u2014 Real-Time-L1**: Zoom, Teams, Meet, WhatsApp calls, STUN, DTLS (explicit appid match)\n\n**Lane 2 \u2014 Hand-on-Control-L2**: SSH, GitHub, GitLab + Remote.Access category (explicit appid + category 7)\n\n**Lane 3 \u2014 Everyday-Response-L3**: Collaboration (Slack, Docs, SharePoint) + GenAI (Claude, ChatGPT) + Email (categories 28, 36, 21)\n\n**Lane 4 \u2014 Background-Bulk-L4**: Cloud.IT (AWS, Azure) + Storage.Backup (Drive, OneDrive) + Social Media + Games (categories 32, 22, 23, 8)\n\n**Note**: Zoom/Teams/WhatsApp also appear under Collaboration category but match Lane 1 first (policy order 1-4, first match wins). GitHub also appears under Storage.Backup but matches Lane 2 first."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "title": "Sessions per Lane (Quantity)",
      "description": "SOURCE: VictoriaMetrics metric fortigate_lane_traffic_session_count, label lane. Derived from Elasticsearch field fortinet.firewall.shapingpolicyname on FortiGate traffic logs (logid 0000000013). Aggregated every 2 minutes by lane_quality_bridge.py. This is ground-truth data directly from FortiGate's shaping policy assignment \u2014 not inferred.",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 5,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 8
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
